<v Daniel X. O'Neil>So, and that was able to show where lobbying money was going. Correct. So, they were able to say, this group donated this amount of money for this cause. Yep. And Paul kind of described that there was something interesting that it wasn't the data. It wasn't what he expected. Some people thought, oh, it was going to be the cigarette groups trying to get, you know, the smoking ban lifted. And it actually turned out to be trying to build hospitals and things like that.

